Subject: [PATCH] a bot logging back in keeps its dungeon finder group

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

PlayerbotHolder::OnBotLogin (src/Bot/PlayerbotMgr.cpp, about line 515 at the
pin below) makes a bot leave any group that holds neither its master nor a
character from a non-random account. That is right for a party a player formed
and walked away from. It is wrong for a dungeon finder group, which the finder
formed for one dungeon and which its members leave by the finder's own exit.

mod-overseer's guild runs are finder groups of five random bots. After a
worldserver restart a random bot has no master, so each member that logged
back in left its group, until the core disbanded it, and the group's instance
bind went with it. Measured on the dev realm at 2026-10-10 14:02 UTC: the core
loaded all four guild runs' finder groups at startup (6 groups, 29 members),
and seconds later only the two family parties were left. Every member came back
in a dungeon instance of its own (Bigmon in instance 10, Chillmon in 5, Deadpan
in 7, Grumbles in 8, all map 36). mod-overseer read each run as disbanded and
ended it, 15 to 49 minutes in.

RandomPlayerbotMgr already makes the same exemption for its own rule ("leave
group if leader is rndbot": `group && !group->isLFGGroup() && ...`). This gives
the login check the same exemption and changes nothing else. A finder group
that really is over is still disbanded by whoever runs it: mod-overseer's stray
pass does that for a guild run that did not survive the restart.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream exempting finder (LFG) groups in PlayerbotHolder::OnBotLogin.

APPLIES TO

mod-playerbots @ 7bae1b5c58c76a0aa20381155edc08096d1485b2, on top of local
patches 0001-0015. Touches only the group check in PlayerbotHolder::OnBotLogin.

diff --git a/src/Bot/PlayerbotMgr.cpp b/src/Bot/PlayerbotMgr.cpp
index b49b848..b4a9868 100644
--- a/src/Bot/PlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/src/Bot/PlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ -512,7 +512,7 @@ void PlayerbotHolder::OnBotLogin(Player* const bot)
             }
         }
 
-        if (!groupValid)
+        if (!groupValid && !group->isLFGGroup())
         {
             botAI->LeaveOrDisbandGroup();
         }
